WEBVTT

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:14.820
<b>Everything Becomes F: The Perfect Insider</b>

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:15.030
<b>Everything Becomes F: The Perfect Insider</b>

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:37.990
<b>Everything Becomes F: The Perfect Insider</b>

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:43.910
<b>Chapter Eight                     Purple Dawn</b>

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:46.500
You saw Dr. Magata?

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:49.340
Yes... It sounded just like her.

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:52.710
And when I asked who she was, she said,

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:55.460
"I've heard that question before."

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:58.940
Who was that?

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:01.100
I'm back...

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:05.770
Do you take milk or sugar, Saikawa-sensei?

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:07.990
Saikawa-sensei takes his black.

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:09.770
I knew it.

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:12.080
Here you go, Saikawa-sensei.

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:13.760
Thank you.

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:15.520
Shimada-san,

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:18.510
where else can you find those machines?

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:21.630
They're all over the lab.

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:23.610
The meeting room on the first floor, for example.

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:28.820
But most people have one in their room, like I do.

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:30.120
I understand.

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:33.580
And if you don't need that sense of floating,

00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:36.880
you don't need the machine.
 You can just do it from a normal terminal.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:40.690
In other words, anyone in the lab

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:43.260
can participate in it, right?

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:46.830
Yes. I just took a look at the login records.

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:51.130
I couldn't identify whom it was that 
Nishinosono-san spoke with,

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:53.980
but there was a new name registered.

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:55.570
What was the name?

00:02:58.480 --> 00:02:59.400
"Michiru."

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:02.340
No way. Could it really be Dr. Magata?

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:04.030
That's impossible!

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:06.130
Then whose body is that?

00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:08.350
But it sounded exactly like her.

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:10.560
Anyone could have done that.

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:13.320
This place uses voice recognition as ID,

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:15.900
and there are also Dr. Magata's interview logs.

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:17.850
So if you put her voice recordings together,

00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:19.740
it would be possible to impersonate her, right?

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:20.920
Correct.

00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:23.300
And a man could do it, as well.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:24.640
Of course.

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:27.960
But that's a pretty elaborate prank.

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:29.760
And a pretty nasty one.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:36.260
Oh, Saikawa-sensei!

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:38.050
Your fingers are so pretty!

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:39.780
Do you get that a lot?

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:43.820
No one's ever complimented them. 
Or insulted them, really.

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:46.990
Oh, I love the way you said that...

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:49.840
Hey, Shimada-san! You're not allowed to do that!

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:52.420
I'm holding back the things I want to say.

00:03:53.270 --> 00:03:55.270
What's wrong with saying what I think?

00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:58.180
It might be the beginning of something special—

00:03:58.180 --> 00:03:59.960
It had better not be!

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:01.740
Shimada-san,

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:04.770
why don't you head back to your room?

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:07.600
I want to talk some more!

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:11.100
I have no spare mental capacity to deal with you.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:14.350
You aren't being elegant at all...

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:15.630
My apologies.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:16.860
Door, close.

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:21.520
Jeez.

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:23.560
It's finally quiet in here.

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:26.410
When you were meeting with Michiru-san...

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:32.510
No, before you were,

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:34.780
I was meeting with Miki-san.

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:37.020
Where is Miki-san?

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:38.970
With the director's wife?

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:41.680
No, the guest room on the first floor.

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:45.450
You were there the whole time, 
until you arrived just now?

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:48.330
Isn't that a little too long?

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:50.090
Hey, Nishinosono-kun...

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:54.150
Do you think Miki-san resembles Dr. Magata?

00:04:54.150 --> 00:04:54.980
Huh?

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:59.310
The employees here plan to try 
to pass her off as Dr. Magata.

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:01.150
They do?

00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:04.800
Well, they're sisters,

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:06.790
so I suppose their faces do look similar...

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:11.330
But Dr. Magata is smaller and thinner.

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:15.470
Miki-san is tall and has a very 
different air about her.

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:16.850
I see.

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:20.850
Tomorrow... No, I suppose it's today now...

00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:22.090
A ship is coming.

00:05:22.330 --> 00:05:25.660
If we can make contact with the mainland, 
the police will be here tonight.

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:30.310
They're going to leave Dr. Magata's 
body in that room.

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:37.780
And they'll tell everyone that 
Miki-san is Dr. Magata.

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:41.480
Normally, Dr. Magata doesn't meet with anyone.

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:45.700
Miki-san will meet with the police

00:05:46.190 --> 00:05:48.460
only if they insist.

00:05:50.150 --> 00:05:53.120
They'll lie for a week.

00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:57.080
But the police will go into that room, right?

00:05:57.460 --> 00:06:00.020
They're going to hide that yellow door.

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:02.720
They'll put a shelf in front of it.

00:06:03.890 --> 00:06:07.090
Nishinosono-kun, we'll be criminals.

00:06:07.730 --> 00:06:10.290
If we don't answer questions, 
we aren't liars, are we?

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:12.720
Is that how your morals work?

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:16.990
But the best option would be 
to tell the police everything,

00:06:16.990 --> 00:06:20.710
and have them keep Dr. Magata's death a secret.

00:06:21.010 --> 00:06:24.190
Then no one would have to lie.

00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:28.040
How would you get them to do that?

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:30.200
I'll ask my uncle.

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:33.000
Oh, right. Your uncle is...

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:35.080
Chief of the Aichi Prefectural Police.

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:39.110
But I don't know if that will work.

00:06:46.490 --> 00:06:47.560
Sensei?

00:07:02.910 --> 00:07:04.010
That's dangerous...

00:07:04.010 --> 00:07:05.290
I'm fine.

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:15.330
You've gotten really bold.

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:20.110
If you had a rope, you could get up or down this.

00:07:20.480 --> 00:07:22.720
It's about six or seven meters, maybe.

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:25.280
I couldn't do it.

00:07:26.740 --> 00:07:29.560
How did the killer get into that room?

00:07:29.830 --> 00:07:32.360
Why kill Dr. Magata?

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:34.600
And how did the killer escape?

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:38.720
We can't answer those questions or 
why Director Shindo was killed...

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:41.550
There may have been different killers.

00:07:42.590 --> 00:07:46.820
Maybe it was two murders, with two 
motives, that happened to coincide.

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:48.250
No way...

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:50.670
That's just weird.

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:53.610
It is weird. Extremely weird.

00:07:54.980 --> 00:07:58.040
Sensei, you're making fun of me, aren't you?

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:02.370
Should we ban weird or strange opinions?

00:08:08.690 --> 00:08:09.840
Forget it.

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:13.550
I've stopped caring about the case.

00:08:14.380 --> 00:08:17.280
I'm enjoying being with you, here and now.

00:08:22.360 --> 00:08:23.740
It's dawn.

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:26.820
This is the start of the day when we become liars.

00:08:28.130 --> 00:08:30.230
So what did you want to talk about?

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:31.400
Right...

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:36.140
A long time ago, I did something 
really terrible to you.

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:40.240
The night of the plane crash.

00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:44.050
I was such a mess. I was out of control.

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:45.540
And I hurt you...

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:50.740
And then, I broke your glasses...

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:54.010
I'm sorry for what I did.

00:08:54.350 --> 00:08:56.780
It's fine. You can fix glasses.

00:08:57.420 --> 00:09:01.340
After that, you came back to
 my house many times.

00:09:02.710 --> 00:09:05.250
I asked you lots of times, didn't I?

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:08.600
"Why do people live?"

00:09:09.850 --> 00:09:10.720
Yeah.

00:09:11.090 --> 00:09:13.660
Back then, it was all you thought about.

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:17.600
Every time I asked, you had a different answer.

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:20.410
And never one I understood.

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:24.170
You once told me that it was to catch goldfish,

00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:26.380
and once, you said the difference

00:09:26.380 --> 00:09:30.350
between meaning and no meaning is like that 
between an eared seal and a fur seal.

00:09:30.350 --> 00:09:31.940
It was all stuff like that.

00:09:34.020 --> 00:09:36.260
"What do you mean, to catch goldfish?"

00:09:36.750 --> 00:09:38.960
At first I got mad, but...

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:42.510
Then it started to seem funny, and eventually...

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:46.790
I was able to laugh.

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:52.020
Why did I forget something so important?

00:09:52.950 --> 00:09:56.030
That's more than enough for now.

00:10:08.650 --> 00:10:11.760
Sorry I'm so busy.

00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:13.980
If you want something to eat, go ahead.

00:10:13.980 --> 00:10:16.190
And if you need a shower...

00:10:16.190 --> 00:10:17.780
Thank you.

00:10:17.780 --> 00:10:20.720
I'll take you up on that shower.

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:23.420
The towels are on the right side of the door—

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:25.450
Yes, thank you.

00:10:27.450 --> 00:10:29.750
If you're going to eat something,

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:31.900
shall I make breakfast?

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:34.530
Would you?

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:38.620
It's been like this the whole time, 
and I haven't eaten anything.

00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:42.520
I'm trying my last resort right now...

00:10:42.520 --> 00:10:44.120
Last resort?

00:10:45.980 --> 00:10:48.120
I'm trying to shut down Red Magic,

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:54.000
and switch over to UNIX.

00:10:54.760 --> 00:10:59.920
Mizutani-kun and Shimada-san are 
making the preparations now.

00:11:00.440 --> 00:11:03.620
It would be simple to just switch over,

00:11:03.940 --> 00:11:08.480
but many of the facility's functions 
are dependent on Red Magic.

00:11:08.860 --> 00:11:12.610
We may not even be able to open the doors.

00:11:12.610 --> 00:11:13.900
Think you can do it?

00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:18.400
Yes, but it'll take another twelve hours or so.

00:11:20.670 --> 00:11:22.980
If this doesn't work,

00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:25.160
I'm really out of options.

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:29.010
So it wasn't a virus that caused

00:11:29.010 --> 00:11:31.040
Red Magic to go out of control?

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:32.190
Correct.

00:11:32.190 --> 00:11:35.330
I never suspected that from the start.

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:38.680
What I suspected was

00:11:38.680 --> 00:11:42.070
a program that had run recently in the system.

00:11:42.370 --> 00:11:44.930
What you call a Trojan...

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:46.840
A Trojan horse.

00:11:47.470 --> 00:11:50.570
What is that, exactly?

00:11:50.570 --> 00:11:55.440
A normal virus attaches itself 
to normal programs and files.

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:59.860
But a Trojan horse makes itself

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:03.790
appear to be a useful program,

00:12:03.790 --> 00:12:08.810
but inside, it contains destructive functions.

00:12:09.110 --> 00:12:13.460
An anti-virus program can't detect it...

00:12:16.780 --> 00:12:20.460
Because it doesn't act irregularly 
and then destroy things.

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:25.640
It destroys things like a virus would, 
as part of its normal operations.

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:28.840
Since it's acting properly, an anti-virus won't work.

00:12:29.420 --> 00:12:32.470
Then you still don't know the cause of the trouble.

00:12:32.470 --> 00:12:35.170
Finding out will take time.

00:12:35.470 --> 00:12:40.420
First, I plan on shutting down the 
system and doing a full reset.

00:12:40.720 --> 00:12:43.350
Giving up on Red Magic

00:12:44.480 --> 00:12:47.490
is the best option I can think of.

00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:50.130
There'll be a lot of obstacles,

00:12:50.130 --> 00:12:53.860
but being unable to contact the 
outside is a critical issue for us.

00:12:53.860 --> 00:12:57.800
We'll have to investigate the 
error's cause afterward.

00:13:15.700 --> 00:13:16.600
Huh?

00:13:17.340 --> 00:13:19.520
I fell asleep, huh?

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:22.390
Yeah. It's almost eleven.

00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:23.870
You're right...

00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:25.950
I slept about three hours.

00:13:26.350 --> 00:13:27.900
The ship will be here soon.

00:13:28.900 --> 00:13:30.530
The police will be contacted,

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:34.830
and then things are likely to get very boring.

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:38.220
I'm fine. I won't be bored.

00:13:38.220 --> 00:13:41.550
Because I'll be with you the whole time, right?

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:44.050
Glad to hear it.

00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:47.260
Since yesterday, I've had so much fun...

00:13:47.990 --> 00:13:49.760
I shouldn't say that, should I?

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:53.180
I was scared, and it was creepy.

00:13:53.860 --> 00:13:56.710
And I was sad, remembering that day.

00:13:57.440 --> 00:14:00.750
But I talked to you about what I remembered,

00:14:01.140 --> 00:14:03.400
and my body feels lighter, somehow.

00:14:04.130 --> 00:14:07.000
If only I could figure out the answer to this quiz,

00:14:07.300 --> 00:14:08.770
everything would be wonderful.

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:12.000
If you call it a quiz, they'll get mad at you.

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:14.210
Two people are dead.

00:14:14.510 --> 00:14:17.120
But that happens all the time, right?

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:20.020
It just happened physically near us.

00:14:21.220 --> 00:14:22.840
You're strange.

00:14:22.840 --> 00:14:25.630
So are you!

00:14:29.770 --> 00:14:31.610
You're in a very good mood.

00:14:32.310 --> 00:14:33.310
I am?

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:35.670
I can tell.

00:14:36.080 --> 00:14:37.990
You've figured something out, haven't you?

00:14:37.990 --> 00:14:38.960
Well...

00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:42.590
It's about F, maybe.

00:14:42.590 --> 00:14:43.590
F?

00:14:43.590 --> 00:14:45.260
"Everything becomes F."

00:14:45.260 --> 00:14:46.610
You figured it out?

00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:47.590
No,

00:14:48.140 --> 00:14:50.390
but I've decided to start thinking about it.

00:14:50.840 --> 00:14:53.540
I think that will lead us to the answer.

00:14:53.930 --> 00:14:58.080
You don't know the answer,
 but you know how to get there?

00:14:58.390 --> 00:15:00.970
My mind must work in a different way than yours.

00:15:01.550 --> 00:15:03.720
I see the path first.

00:15:04.260 --> 00:15:07.090
And then I slowly travel down it.

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:08.900
That's weird...

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:11.350
F, huh?

00:15:11.690 --> 00:15:16.730
Finish. Future. Free. Or...

00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:19.430
Future?

00:15:19.430 --> 00:15:20.980
"Miki" means "Future"?

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:24.040
See? That's how your brain works.

00:15:24.490 --> 00:15:28.310
You take random ideas you think of and 
try to use them to find the answer.

00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:30.990
But that isn't right.

00:15:31.710 --> 00:15:35.070
"Shiki" means "Four seasons," 
which also begins with F.

00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:38.220
And "Michiru" can mean "Full," 
which also has an "F."

00:15:38.570 --> 00:15:41.770
I'm more interested in "Everything" than "F."

00:15:42.220 --> 00:15:45.420
Does she mean her four personalities?

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:49.130
That would mean the subject 
should be "everyone," right?

00:15:49.680 --> 00:15:53.120
There must be a reason it's "everything."

00:15:54.500 --> 00:15:56.490
<i>Final notice to all staff.</i>

00:15:56.810 --> 00:15:59.970
<i>At exactly 11:00, the main system will shut down.</i>

00:15:59.970 --> 00:16:03.370
<i>All functionality will be off-line 
for approximately ten minutes.</i>

00:16:03.690 --> 00:16:05.630
They're shutting down Red Magic?

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:07.730
That was faster than I thought.

00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:09.970
I hope it doesn't shut off the electricity.

00:16:16.090 --> 00:16:18.980
Nishinosono-kun, you said

00:16:19.380 --> 00:16:21.830
Dr. Magata wore gloves, right?

00:16:21.830 --> 00:16:22.780
Yes.

00:16:22.780 --> 00:16:24.100
Why?

00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:25.570
I don't know...

00:16:26.230 --> 00:16:30.920
Wait, don't you wear gloves when 
you wear a wedding dress?

00:16:31.250 --> 00:16:33.880
But the body had no hands.

00:17:12.020 --> 00:17:13.800
Who are you?

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:21.490
I won't let you do this!

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:25.150
But Dr. Magata is smaller and thinner.

00:17:25.530 --> 00:17:29.370
Miki-san is tall and has a very 
different air about her.

00:17:29.690 --> 00:17:32.940
Seven is the only lonely number.

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:36.400
I am the only one that is seven.

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:49.020
Sensei, what's wrong?

00:17:49.020 --> 00:17:51.770
Imperfection, attempting to become perfect.

00:17:52.400 --> 00:17:53.460
Sensei?

00:17:55.150 --> 00:17:56.120
I'm fine.

00:17:56.700 --> 00:17:57.970
I want to smoke.

00:17:58.500 --> 00:18:00.100
Can you let go of my hand?

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:21.740
What are you doing?

00:18:21.740 --> 00:18:24.660
I've figured out a little bit of the truth.

00:18:25.680 --> 00:18:27.390
Tell me, Sensei!

00:18:27.710 --> 00:18:28.940
Sensei!

00:18:35.560 --> 00:18:36.760
Nishinosono-kun...

00:18:36.760 --> 00:18:37.800
Yes?

00:18:38.700 --> 00:18:41.800
It wasn't Dr. Magata you saw.

00:18:45.470 --> 00:18:46.410
The lights are back!

00:19:04.130 --> 00:19:07.250
It's connecting! The phones work!

00:19:09.150 --> 00:19:11.630
Hello. This is the Nishinosono residence.

00:19:11.630 --> 00:19:13.450
Suwano, it's me.

00:19:13.450 --> 00:19:15.360
There's been a problem. Get here now.

00:19:15.360 --> 00:19:17.920
There's been a murder at Magata Labs...

00:19:18.670 --> 00:19:20.340
Call my uncle!

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:21.860
I want you to contact the police, too!

00:19:21.860 --> 00:19:23.130
Miss...

00:19:23.460 --> 00:19:26.420
Miss, are you hurt?

00:19:26.420 --> 00:19:27.680
Oh, not now...

00:19:27.940 --> 00:19:29.180
I'm hanging up.

00:19:29.180 --> 00:19:30.790
I see.

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:35.570
I'll contact the police immediately, then.

00:19:38.390 --> 00:19:40.000
We finally got through.

00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:42.210
Sensei, about what you were just saying...

00:19:42.210 --> 00:19:44.070
Yeah. Want me to tell you?

00:19:44.070 --> 00:19:46.860
No, I'll think for myself.

00:19:47.400 --> 00:19:51.170
I'll catch up to you on my own.

00:19:52.720 --> 00:19:55.310
You've gotten strong.

00:20:03.690 --> 00:20:07.460
<i>After the incident, Shiki was arrested.</i>

00:20:08.890 --> 00:20:11.140
<i>There was a trial, eventually,</i>

00:20:11.620 --> 00:20:13.950
<i>but she was declared</i> non compos mentis

00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:16.180
<i>and therefore, not guilty.</i>

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:19.440
<b>Nagono Juvenile Detention Center</b>

00:20:25.970 --> 00:20:30.140
<i>And so, Shiki cut herself off 
from the outside world,</i>

00:20:31.580 --> 00:20:34.510
<i>and lived inside her lab.</i>

00:20:35.940 --> 00:20:39.520
<i>Some said it was the same 
as being inside a prison.</i>

00:20:41.110 --> 00:20:42.070
<i>However,</i>

00:20:42.500 --> 00:20:45.650
<i>it was the environment Shiki wanted.</i>

00:20:46.850 --> 00:20:48.470
<i>Meeting no one</i>

00:20:49.420 --> 00:20:51.450
<i>and being seen by no one.</i>

00:20:56.580 --> 00:20:58.980
Michiru, unlock the door.

00:21:11.410 --> 00:21:13.070
<i>With no one interfering</i>

00:21:13.850 --> 00:21:16.070
<i>and no one telling her to do anything.</i>

00:21:17.730 --> 00:21:18.650
<i>That was</i>

00:21:19.590 --> 00:21:22.020
<i>the ideal world</i>

00:21:22.550 --> 00:21:24.340
<i>she'd always desired.</i>
